## 5. Experiments

**Setup.** Model: Qwen3-0.6B (matches the only prior real-NPU ZO work, MobiZO, enabling a
direct same-model comparison) and OPT-2.7B (matches FZOO's and P-GAP's own literature
setting, for algorithmic validation and rank/target ablation before deployment). Task:
SST-2 throughout; RTE as a harder-task check. Platforms: Hexagon NPU (v81, unrestricted HVX),
matched CPU fallback, and GPU (both models, for algorithm development and hyperparameter
search — on-device search is infeasible at mobile-hardware iteration speed, so every
on-device hyperparameter is chosen on GPU first and deployed unchanged).

**Table 1 — GPU target-ablation (OPT-2.7B, SST-2, 5000 steps, matched hyperparameters
otherwise).** The single largest lever found in this study, larger than rank or learning
rate:

