## 6. Limitations

Stated plainly, matching the standard this project holds its own internal documentation to:

- **Sample-count mismatch between Tables 3 and 4.** The on-device numbers in Table 4 were
  measured at N=500 training examples; the GPU comparison against MobiZO (Table 3) uses
  N=1000, matching MobiZO's own protocol. These are not directly comparable to each other
  without re-running Table 4's numbers at N=1000 — flagged explicitly rather than implied
  away. `[PENDING: N=1000 re-run of the Table 4 baselines]`.
- **No full-model (no-subspace, no-adapter) FZOO GPU reference exists for Qwen3-0.6B** —
  only OPT-2.7B has that comparison point (Table 2). The Qwen3-0.6B story (Table 3) currently
  compares subspace-restricted variants against MobiZO's own numbers, not against an
  unrestricted ceiling on the same model.
- **The attention-target result is GPU-validated only at time of writing** — its on-device
  NPU counterpart is mid-relaunch after a target-matching bug (a broad substring match
  unintentionally included two 1D normalization vectors per layer alongside the four real
  attention weight matrices) was found and fixed. The GPU number (Table 1, Table 3) is not
  yet confirmed to transfer to real hardware.
- **The CPU/NPU crossover's exact rank threshold is based on two measured points** (r=8,
  r=256), not yet a full sweep — in progress, see Figure 1.
- **RTE (a harder GLUE task) has not yet been re-run at the corrected configuration** — an
  earlier attempt used the feed-forward-only target and the pre-sweep learning rate/eps
  convention, both since found suboptimal, and showed a peak-then-decline trajectory rather
  than the monotonic convergence seen on SST-2; not yet re-tested with the corrected config.

